    "abstract": null,
    "field": "Extinction risk from climate change",
    "problem": "Assessing global extinction risk from climate change is challenging because traditional models based on habitat loss must be adapted to project individual species\u2019 complex range shifts and uncertain dispersal abilities under future climate scenarios.",
    "method": "We propose a method that applies the species-area relationship to projected losses in the climatically suitable ranges of species to estimate the percentage of species that will be committed to extinction under future climate change scenarios.",
    "task": "The task is to assess future extinction risks for a large sample of species by projecting their geographical distributions under various climate change scenarios and then using species-area relationships to estimate the proportion of species that will be committed to extinction.",
